        <item>
            <title>2.8-rc.1</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:34:13 +0000</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/TheBoredTeam/boring.notch/releases</link>
            <sparkle:channel>beta</sparkle:channel>
            <sparkle:version>282</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.8-rc.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description>&lt;!-- &lt;h2&gt;✨ What's New&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;🎵 Music &amp;amp; Media&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compact player&lt;/strong&gt; – Added a compact, player-focused layout for the opened notch with playback, shuffle, and media-output controls.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remaining time&lt;/strong&gt; – Added an option to show remaining playback time instead of duration.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Now Playing reliability&lt;/strong&gt; – Improved availability detection, fallback behavior, connection recovery, and user-facing recovery notices when Now Playing is unavailable.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Artwork reliability&lt;/strong&gt; – Fixed artwork disappearing during lightweight Now Playing updates and stale artwork caused by Safari Private Browsing and browser helper processes. — @rogedev, @SpaceCypher&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YouTube Music / Pear&lt;/strong&gt; – Improved observer persistence, WebSocket reconnection, connection-state handling, and authentication compatibility. — @cjuriartec&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lyrics&lt;/strong&gt; – Synced lyrics now follow their actual playback timing for smoother line-by-line scrolling.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real-time audio waveform&lt;/strong&gt; – Added a waveform visualizer option that uses real-time captured audio on supported macOS versions (14.2+), and significantly improved the performance of the original visualizer.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamic audio output&lt;/strong&gt; – You can now control the active audio route, including speakers, wired headphones, AirPods, Bluetooth devices, and external outputs. — @colinchambachan&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Media gestures&lt;/strong&gt; – Added horizontal gestures for media controls and improved gesture behavior across the music area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;📅 Calendar &amp;amp; Reminders&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Weekly calendar view&lt;/strong&gt; – Added an optional week-based calendar view with a configurable week start: System, Sunday, or Monday. — @TemujinCalidius&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join meetings from events&lt;/strong&gt; – Calendar events can detect supported meeting links and open them directly from the notch. Supports Google Meet, Zoom, Microsoft Teams, Webex, Whereby, and Jitsi. — @Subhanshu20101&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Calendar navigation&lt;/strong&gt; – Added vertical scroll navigation for the date picker and improved week-based navigation behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reminder date reliability&lt;/strong&gt; – Improved all-day reminder handling across local time zones and daylight-saving boundaries so reminders retain their correct calendar date.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;🎛️ OSD (formerly HUD) &amp;amp; System Controls&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Renamed HUD to OSD&lt;/strong&gt; – Now uses the more appropriate term in English, which was already used in some localizations.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Smoother brightness control&lt;/strong&gt; – Brightness adjustments now use smoother stepping with reduced jumps and improved hold behavior. — @benjaminfrombe&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BetterDisplay &amp;amp; Lunar&lt;/strong&gt; – Added and improved real-time brightness event streaming and control through external display providers.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key reliability&lt;/strong&gt; – Improved key interception and recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audio and display routing&lt;/strong&gt; – Improved handling of built-in and external display/control sources and their availability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;🔔 Notification Mirroring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Notifications in the notch&lt;/strong&gt; – Mirrors visible notification banners in the notch with the sending application's icon.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;App filtering&lt;/strong&gt; – Choose whether to mirror notifications from all apps or only selected applications.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Notification queue&lt;/strong&gt; – Multiple incoming notifications can now be queued and browsed from the expanded notification.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Closed-notch indicator&lt;/strong&gt; – New notification activity feedback appears while the notch is closed.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Notification reliability&lt;/strong&gt; – Improved banner discovery, XPC delivery, focus handling, stale-banner handling, and Notification Center interaction.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accessibility-aware mirroring&lt;/strong&gt; – Notification mirroring now checks Accessibility authorization in real time and provides a direct way to grant access when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;🔋 Battery&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Charging wattage&lt;/strong&gt; – Shows the connected power adapter's reported wattage in the battery popover. — @isaacau502&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Time until empty&lt;/strong&gt; – Added a battery discharge estimate alongside time to full charge. — @lasersushi&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Better charge formatting&lt;/strong&gt; – Charge estimates now use localized hour/minute formatting instead of a raw minute count. — @lasersushi&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Battery health&lt;/strong&gt; – Improved maximum-capacity detection and correctly handles cases where battery-health information is unavailable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;📦 Shelf&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;More reliable Shelf interactions&lt;/strong&gt; – Improved selection, hit testing, multi-item dragging, context menus, double-click behavior, and Quick Look synchronization.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reverse Shelf ordering&lt;/strong&gt; – Added an option to keep newer Shelf items at the front. — @yannip1234&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shelf controls&lt;/strong&gt; – Added the ability to disable Shelf behavior entirely when it is not needed.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sharing improvements&lt;/strong&gt; – Improved Quick Share provider discovery and application-icon handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;📷 Camera &amp;amp; Mirror&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improved camera reliability&lt;/strong&gt; – Reworked the camera for increased reliability, particularly on multiple-display setups.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Camera recovery&lt;/strong&gt; – Improved permission handling, camera selection, disconnect/reconnect recovery, interruption handling, sleep/wake recovery, and display lifecycle management.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Camera selection&lt;/strong&gt; – Added camera selection for the Mirror feature, with an Automatic mode that prefers the built-in camera. — @ReubenCowell&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mirror controls&lt;/strong&gt; – Added a setting to switch between mirrored and natural camera output. — @anmolmalhotra97&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;⚙️ Settings &amp;amp; Appearance&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reworked Settings navigation&lt;/strong&gt; – Settings are now organized into dedicated sections for Notch, Appearance, Media, Calendar, Shelf, Mirror, Battery, OSD, Notifications, Shortcuts, and About.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dedicated Notch settings&lt;/strong&gt; – Added a dedicated Notch section for sizing, hover behavior, gestures, animation, and window behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Appearance controls&lt;/strong&gt; – Moved accent-color customization into Appearance and expanded custom accent-color options.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Animation control&lt;/strong&gt; – Added a setting to control the notch opening-animation speed. — @Amorfx&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language selection&lt;/strong&gt; – Added an in-app language selector with a restart prompt when required.&lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bug report button&lt;/strong&gt; – Added an in-app bug report button in the About section which opens the GitHub Issue form page with app version and os version pre-filled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;🔄 Software Updates&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update channels&lt;/strong&gt; – Added channel-aware update support for Stable, Beta, and Nightly builds, with the available channels determined by the current build. — @notluquis&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Safer updates&lt;/strong&gt; – Improved the updater with additional installer security improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;🚀 Accessibility &amp;amp; Onboarding&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;macOS 27 compatibility&lt;/strong&gt; – Accessibility permission references now use the current macOS terminology (Device Control and Data Access) and localization, with a fallback for compatibility.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improved permission checks&lt;/strong&gt; – Accessibility-dependent features now properly check authorization instead of sometimes relying on stale permission state.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improved onboarding&lt;/strong&gt; – Refined permission handling and onboarding flows, including audio-capture permission setup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;🛠️ Fixes &amp;amp; Improvements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Fixed Shelf files being dragged into WhatsApp as text paths instead of actual file attachments. — @ShehanCes&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Fixed inconsistent Home ↔ Shelf tab-switch animations. — @ShehanCes&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Fixed album art alignment in the live activity view&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Fixed calendar month/year alignment and expanded the clickable area for calendar dates. — @mlbonniec&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Fixed Apple Music favorite actions. — @karadoganyi&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Normalized notch gesture direction when macOS Natural Scrolling is disabled. — @karadoganyi&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Fixed long Quick Share provider names not being centered correctly. — @daemonsloth&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Fixed notch content being vertically offset on some displays. — @KoukeNeko&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Fixed the DMG background lookup and clarified the copy-to-Applications installation flow.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Removed the deprecated Homebrew quarantine-installation flag and updated related installation guidance. — @ftery0&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Improved locale-aware formatting across settings, battery, OSD, progress indicators, and accessibility labels.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Improved localization coverage for media controls, Shelf actions, native dialogs, and settings.&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Improved concurrency safety, lifecycle management, and internal architecture to reduce races, retain cycles, and unnecessary background work. — @Dbhardwaj99&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Updated dependencies used by the project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;👋 New Contributors&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;@adam-dziuk · @karadoganyi · @benjaminfrombe · @daemonsloth · @mlbonniec · @KoukeNeko · @Amorfx · @ftery0 · @anmolmalhotra97 · @colinchambachan · @ReubenCowell · @cjuriartec · @lasersushi · @Etzeo · @yannip1234 · @TemujinCalidius · @ShehanCes · @isaacau502 · @SpaceCypher · @morriisan · @Dbhardwaj99 · @rogedev · @Subhanshu20101 · @notluquis&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thank you to everyone who contributed code, translations, testing, bug reports, and feedback to this release!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;📄 Full Changelog&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/TheBoredTeam/boring.notch/compare/v2.7.3...v2.8-rc.0"&gt;Compare v2.7.3 → v2.8-rc.0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; --&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;🛠️ Fixes &amp;amp; Improvements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Fixed performance issues causing high CPU utilization for some users — @DavideSirico and @Alexander5015&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Fixed mirror sizing and alignment&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Fixed UI bugs with notifications&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Fixed Audio output selector hover broken and improved design &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Renamed boringNotch to Boring Notch&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;Updated dependencies used by the project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;👋 New Contributors&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;@DavideSirico&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thank you to everyone who contributed code, translations, testing, bug reports, and feedback to this release!&lt;/p&gt;

